eu fisheries ministers have reached  agreement on the maximum number of fish  that can be caught for certain species  in the baltic sea  the political accord reached during  talks in luxembourg  means that almost all stocks in the  baltic will be fished at sustainable  levels from next year  i believe this agreement will serve as a  good basis  for the council in december when we will  have to agree on fishing opportunities  in the other eu and non-eu waters  today's compromised is balanced and  based  on the agreement at the regional level  scientific advice and multi-annual  baltic cod management plan  the fishing opportunities in the baltic  sea concern five species  cod herring place salmon and sprat  with more fish stocks managed at  sustainable levels it will be possible  to raise catches for some species in  certain fishing zones  the decision means that the catch limits  data is likely to be made available to  fishermen by the first of january next  year this agreement only involves eu  member states in the baltic sea region
 

